# Shell scripts are run by bash, including on Windows, and bash will not run a
# script with carriage returns in it: `$'\r': command not found`, on line 1.
# A clone with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default — produces
# exactly that, so the self-hoster following docs/self-hosting.md would find
# `server/scripts/smoke.sh` broken before they ever reached Cloudflare.
*.sh text eol=lf
